# fixedbugs, defect 396, lane b13-land-buf, 2026-10-07: the twin of
# `fixedbugs-396-sha256-final-into-one-cell-aborts` on a header of the
# program's own, so every platform runs it. `digest32` writes 32 bytes, bound
# as one cell; the local lent to it lives against a page nothing may touch
# (panel 196's R7), and C writing its second byte is named.
extern "fixedbugs-396-buffers.h"
    function digest32(@md: u8) -> i32

function main()
    m: u8 @ 0
    print("before")
    print(digest32(@m))
    print("not reached ", m)
